  "notes": "{発射|はっしゃ} means firing, shooting, or launching — used for projectiles, weapons, rockets, and missiles.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {発射|はっしゃ}する: to fire, to launch\n- {発射|はっしゃ}ボタン: launch button\n- {発射|はっしゃ}{台|だい}: launch pad\n- ミサイル{発射|はっしゃ}: missile launch\n- ロケット{発射|はっしゃ}: rocket launch\n- {発射|はっしゃ}{音|おん}: firing sound\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n{発車|はっしゃ} means departure of a vehicle (train, bus). Same pronunciation, completely different meaning — a common source of confusion for learners.\n\nRELATED:\n- {打|う}ち{上|あ}げる: also used for rocket launches (less technical)\n- {射撃|しゃげき}: shooting, marksmanship",
